  "title": "On the overlap of transcription factor binding and regulatory targets: functional and regulatory coherence of top-bound targets is masked by weakly bound ones",
  "doi": "10.1101/2025.10.12.681120",
  "abstract": "A recent study that systematically mapped genomic bindings and regulatory effects of transcription factors (TFs) reported a surprisingly low overlap between TF binding and regulatory targets in Saccharomyces cerevisiae 1 . Our analysis suggests that this conclusion depends on the permissive definition of binding targets, which includes a large fraction of weakly bound sites.",
